# Wave W17-AB (Route 224): head turf — stone-coast turf, flower flecks: a sage coastal green carrying white and pale-yellow flower flecks and sparse stone-grey grit — the meadow the champion’s road runs through, thickening toward the flower field at the Foamline end (design: flowers beyond counting at the far end of the path; the turf takes their first flecks). Route 224’s own ground — split from its twin Foamline Path by element entire (the dry stone coast vs the plank road over water — Foamline ships no ground register) and from Route 213’s salt turf by register: this turf is flowered meadow, that one salt flat.
